----- Robert Otterson -----

    SWCC (Storage Works Command Console ) would most likely be what your
lohing for.
           You can interface with NT/UNIX/VMS (&other) Storage if it is
installed.
            The UNIX system has an "agent(s)"  and an INTEL PC has the front
end.


----- David Hull -----

try hszterm, I believe it comes with swcc, which is a free download from
compaq.  Gives you access to all CLI commands from the UNIX command line.

Cheers,
David Hull


----- Alan -----

A future version of SWCC is supposed to a scripting feature
to replace the need for HSZterm.  As far as I know those are
the only two choices.  If SWCC isn't an adequate solution
for you, then you'll want to save that HSZterm kit and
