From tru64-unix-managers  Thu Apr 29 13:08:18 1999
From: Matthew Huff <mhuff () ox ! com>
Date: Thu, 29 Apr 1999 13:08:18 +0000
To: tru64-unix-managers
Subject: SUMMARY:  Byte swapping on Digital Unix
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=96079040316018

1) No, we can't get rid of the Sparc and migrate it to alpha. The
   third-party market data software only runs on Sparc Solaris.

2) XDR and other solutions aren't the answer. XDR abstracts byte
   swapping. We want to get rid of it. The recent rapid increase
   in market volume has swamped up. Yes, we do have EV6 systems,
   but the byte swapping is wasting large number of CPU cycles.

3) As we thought, the alpha can run in either endian mode (most
   "new" chips can, but the SRM firmware and expansion boards
   require little endian mode. 

