Many thanks to:

Joe Fletcher
Danielle Georgette
Bell Jonathan
Alan Davis
John Klapp
Tom Webster
Mathew Huff

The concensus is to  install the PPP Protocol  on both sides of the
connection, this will allow me to establish a TCP/IP link between both
sides, 
as the X11 system is basically a network-based protocol and does not allow
for
direct serial port connections.

Other possibility if network traffic is the concern is to install a second
network card.
or to connect the machines to a switching equipment

Rodrigo Poblete
