From tru64-unix-managers  Tue Apr 27 18:13:09 1999
From: Tony Warner <Tony.Warner () gat ! com>
Date: Tue, 27 Apr 1999 18:13:09 +0000
To: tru64-unix-managers
Subject: SUMMARY: XDMCP session with C2 security enabled
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=96079040315973

Thanks to all who responded!
Bruce Senn
Oyanarte Portilho
Oisin McGuinness

The answer had to do with adding entries for the X terminal
in the /etc/auth/system/ttys and /etc/auth/system/devassign
files. I followed the instructions in the faq (thanks Oisin)
(www.unix.digital.com/unix/faq/graphics.html#G4) but still
had problems. Then Bruce suggested using wildcards ('*')in the entries
instead of the actual hostname.  That did the trick. Obviously,
this means that any host can start an xdm session, but I am not
too concerned about that at the moment.

Thanks for all the help...

Tony Warner

