Original Problem:

A multi-volume tar archive cannot be restored on an existing 4100 using a
TZ88 tape drive, but CAN be restored on a "twin" machine (same O/S,
patches) using a TZ89.

Thanks to

Dr. Tom Blinn
alan@nabeth.cxo.dec.com

But the big winner goes to Serguei Patchkovskii, who figured out that the
machine I was having the problem on seemed to be using GNU tar rather than
the standard tar that comes with Digital UNIX, and that GNU tar has a bug
that doesn't allow multi-volume archives to work. 

