From tru64-unix-managers  Mon Apr 12 11:22:40 1999
From: Kiyoshi Yoda <yoda () ele ! crl ! melco ! co ! jp>
Date: Mon, 12 Apr 1999 11:22:40 +0000
To: tru64-unix-managers
Subject: SUMMARY:  how to configure a replaced Ethernet card
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=96079040315611

First of all, I would like to say thanks to the 5 people who quickly responded me.

The original question: 
   I have just replaced my DE435 EtherWORKS PCI (10base) with
   DE500-BA Fast EtherWORKS PCI (10/100 base).
   When I reboot the OS 4.0a, I saw a message saying that network is unreachable.

The most detailed reply from Gerhald Norte suggested me to type
boot -file genvmunix and doconfig (with no option), then move the new kernel to /vmunix. 

As a matter of fact, the key issue was that DE500-BA does not work with 4.0a, and
works with 4.0d. This was mentioned in 4.0d installation manual, not in the DE500-BA manual!
So this is not a genvmunix issue, but OS compatibility issue. However, I carelessly unplugged the
card before updating the OS. So I could confirm that the above procedure works very well  (^_^).

To summarize, 
(1) to install a new hardware, boot -file genvmunix and doconfig (with no option), 
      then move the new kernel to /vmunix.
(2) to use DE500-BA, update OS to 4.0d . Don't forget update firmware.

I learned a lot and thanks again,

Kiyoshi



