Subject: SUMMARY: Compaq SURVEY: use of V4.0 system adminstration applications
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=96079040315580

The survey asked if the recipient used the Tru64 UNIX V4.0 system
administration applications, and, if so, how often.

I received 102 responses! 90 of the respondents noted that they use
one or more of the apps. Only 12 of the 102 responses stated that
they never use any. (Of those, four stated that they didn't even know 
they existed. The remaining 8 stated they are hard-core UNIX
experts who only use the command line.)

Here are the results in order of most used to least used for the
90 system managers who stated that they use the apps:

Application		Uses It        Often  Sometimes  Infrequently

Kernel Tuner            78              24      35          19
Account Manager         72              31      25          16
System Information      66              20      25          21
License Manager         62              12      30          20
Process Tuner           40               8      21          11
Host Manager            32               5      11          16
Power Manager           31               1      10          20
Display Window          27               4       7          16
File Sharing            27               2      10          15
Shutdown                15               2       8           5
Archiver                11               1       4           6

Note that the frequency designation is often misleading. Some apps
lend themselves to be used infrequently, like Power Manager or File
Sharing which are mainly "set and forget" type applications.

Thank you all for your responses. This information is extremely
valuable to the UNIX Engineering group. Thanks especially to Dave Sill,
the "keeper" of this list, for clearing access to this list for these 
valuable surveys.

