Subject: SUMMARY: mountd capabilities
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=96079040315449

Hi all,

My problem was to export a directory with different access rights for different
hosts. Thanks to Peter Stern <peter@tov.weizmann.ac.il> for the answer. The
solution is:
/filesystem -root=... -rw=...
Anybody not listed can mount read-only.

The ... stands stands for a colon separated list of hosts. Hosts wich need root
r/w access must occur in both lists (that was my real problem).

Regards

  Peter Wuestner

