From tru64-unix-managers  Thu Apr 01 13:54:58 1999
From: Rolf-Peter Kienzle <kienzlep () uni-freiburg ! de>
Date: Thu, 01 Apr 1999 13:54:58 +0000
To: tru64-unix-managers
Subject: SUMMARY: ZLXp support on PW433au under Unix 4.0c
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=96079040315410

Hello managers!

Thanks to

       Graham Allan <ALLAN@mnhep1.hep.umn.edu>
       Joe Fletcher <joe@meng.ucl.ac.uk>
       Paul Watson <phwatso@cooper-energy-services.com>
       Arnold Sutter <Arnold.Sutter@udt.ch>

for responding so quickly!

The original question was 

"Does anybody out there know whether the ZLXp-L1,L2 graphics adapters
are supported in a PW433au under Unix V4.0C?"

The overwhelmingly simple answer is

"No, they aren't. Not supported by the hardware!"

Moreover, these adapters are supported on other machines up to Tru64
Unix 4.0E and Open3D V4.9 only. As a result, an ELSA Gloria Synergy
should run fine with Tru64 Unix 4.0D AND Open3D V4.9 or Tru64 Unix V4.0E
(with or without Open3D) in a PW433au.

Regards

Peter

